quisite-consistency"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Prerequisite: 'Eval-run callers MUST construct `LLMConfig(repo_path=pinned.config_root)` so `fallback_targets_for`'s lookup ... resolves against the fallback-free ephemeral config'","Prerequisite: `PASS_MODEL_CLASS = {\"pass1\": \"frontier\", \"pass2\": \"standard\"}`; check_cache_effective is the caching-confirmation instrument","Subject makes no reference to `parity.resolve_pinned_model`, `PinnedModel`, `check_cache_effective`, or `LLMConfig(repo_path=pinned.config_root)`; it resolves the model via `sizing.largest_window_tokens(standard_class_model)` directly"],"finding":"The subject bypasses the parity module's fallback-free pinning mechanism. The parity prerequisite states eval-run callers MUST construct `LLMConfig(repo_path=pinned.config_root)` (from `resolve_pinned_model(\"pass2\")`) so that `fallback_targets_for`'s lookup resolves against a fallback-free ephemeral config, otherwise `PydanticAIRunner.run` re-derives the Anthropic-direct fallback chain from the resolved model string and collapses `prompt_cache_style` to `none`. The subject's replay instead calls `verify_findings(..., window_tokens=sizing.largest_window_tokens(standard_class_model))` via `RunRequest.for_structured(..., bounds=RunRequest.INHERIT_POLICY)` with no mention of `resolve_pinned_model`, `PinnedModel.config_root`, or an ephemeral fallback-free config. It also does not use `stamp_pass_model`/`refuse_diff_on_model_mismatch`/`check_cache_effective`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd356ee23c6fdf8f3","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Production input, byte-identical — exact seam call","norm_id":"n297e45ea076d722b","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited